{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Archaeology (why the existing gate missed these): scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py (policy d37e, commit 6739ea54fa) passes CLEAN on the current tree. Its policy sanctions git_adapter.py/_ref_lock.py at MODULE granularity, so callers composing the exported primitives (git_adapter.add at reconcile_helpers.py:226 + git_adapter.commit at :246 — no lock, no atomic commit+push) are approved call-by-call. Gate enforces the mechanism rule (no raw subprocess git) but not the protocol rule (mutations via the atomic transaction). Fix = R3 composition rule in the EXISTING checker; description rewritten accordingly."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786808315626180001,"uuid":"8a54ff8e-5b65-40a3-bf5d-dffcf1e732a5"}